This is such a great book.

00:04:27.130 --> 00:04:30.100
So this is the final book in
your children's series, right?

00:04:30.100 --> 00:04:32.130
- I was asked to write a
middle grade fiction book

00:04:32.130 --> 00:04:34.440
and I said I do it if I
could write four of them

00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:35.870
and I wanted to write about magic,

00:04:35.870 --> 00:04:37.500
and I wanted to write about kids

00:04:37.500 --> 00:04:40.180
'cause I have two of them,
and I love the father

00:04:40.180 --> 00:04:42.130
And so I wanted to write something

00:04:42.130 --> 00:04:43.210
that had to do with real magic

00:04:43.210 --> 00:04:46.220
'cause I love magic, cards
and coins and an illusion

00:04:46.220 --> 00:04:51.220
not Potter magic and wands and
wizards and things like that.

00:04:51.870 --> 00:04:52.940
And so that's what I did.

00:04:52.940 --> 00:04:55.190
And each book Chronicle
is one of these four kids

00:04:55.190 --> 00:04:57.320
that lives in a fictional
town called Mineral Wells

00:04:57.320 --> 00:04:59.590
and each book is through the perspective

00:04:59.590 --> 00:05:01.860
of one of those kids and so
we're at the fourth book.

00:05:01.860 --> 00:05:04.320
It's a girl named Ridley Larsen.

00:05:04.320 --> 00:05:06.770
She's a wheelchair bound,
awesome, amazing chick

00:05:06.770 --> 00:05:10.770
who is all about transformation,

00:05:10.770 --> 00:05:12.630
turning one thing into another thing.

00:05:12.630 --> 00:05:14.950
You see the book even
looks like a playing card.

00:05:14.950 --> 00:05:16.071
All four look like that.

00:05:16.071 --> 00:05:19.410
So she's super amazing
dealing with her mom,

00:05:19.410 --> 00:05:20.990
dealing with her stresses

00:05:20.990 --> 00:05:23.180
and figuring out who the the evil guy is

00:05:23.180 --> 00:05:26.930
in this awful magic group
called the Emerald Ring,

00:05:26.930 --> 00:05:29.560
who's disbanded them, who's
burned the magic shop down

00:05:29.560 --> 00:05:31.610
and this is the final story

00:05:31.610 --> 00:05:33.010
where it all kind of comes together

00:05:33.010 --> 00:05:36.090
and we learn all the
things we needed to know.

00:05:36.090 --> 00:05:38.550
The book has teachers
magic tricks within it.

00:05:38.550 --> 00:05:40.300
So if you wanna learn some magic tricks,

00:05:40.300 --> 00:05:41.360
each book has four or five

00:05:41.360 --> 00:05:42.680
different teacher tricks throughout.

00:05:42.680 --> 00:05:45.550
There's codes, there's
puzzles, there's ciphers.

00:05:45.550 --> 00:05:47.780
So I really respect readers, respect kids,

00:05:47.780 --> 00:05:50.900
and I'm so stoked that
the books have done well

00:05:50.900 --> 00:05:52.740
and I hope this one continues to trend.

00:05:52.740 --> 00:05:54.780
- Yeah, no, it's obviously
done well, how innovative?

00:05:54.780 --> 00:05:56.700
That's so cool to make them
like a part of the story,

00:05:56.700 --> 00:05:57.860
they get to learn stuff from the book

00:05:57.860 --> 00:06:00.058
and like kinda be part of
it, that's really cool.

00:06:00.058 --> 00:06:00.950
- Definitely.
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:06:00.950 --> 00:06:01.950
- You like magic, right?

00:06:01.950 --> 00:06:06.950
- I love magic and I
actually hurt like I am child

00:06:07.270 --> 00:06:09.700
when people do magic in
front of me, it's annoying.

00:06:09.700 --> 00:06:12.520
But you also created a
magical board game I heard,

00:06:12.520 --> 00:06:13.470
is that real?

00:06:13.470 --> 00:06:18.470
- That is real as well,
I love buying the games,

00:06:18.470 --> 00:06:20.680
but I always find that
they're party games.

00:06:20.680 --> 00:06:21.658
You know that they're--

00:06:21.658 --> 00:06:22.581
